# Generated training artefacts. `prepared/` is a full materialised copy of the
# dataset and `runs/` holds checkpoints; `annotations/` holds every image copied
# into a tagging batch. None of it belongs in version control, and on a
# OneDrive-synced checkout all of it would otherwise be uploaded.
runs/
prepared/
datasets/
annotations/
weights/

# Model files, wherever they land. These are hundreds of megabytes each and
# GitHub rejects anything over 100 MB.
*.pt
*.onnx
*.engine
*.npy

# Ultralytics writes a label cache beside each prepared split. It is derived,
# and a stale one has caused a run to train on the wrong image set.
*.cache

# Secrets and machine-specific configuration. `.env` holds the dataset paths for
# one particular machine; `.env.example` is the committed template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.service.example

# Written by the image build, recording the exact resolved dependency versions.
requirements.lock.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Editors and tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# OS and OneDrive litter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Assistant context. CLAUDE.md carries the project's invariants and the
# reasoning behind them; keep it local rather than in the repository.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.copilot/
